mapping "M488A.1" source="M488A" target="83561009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source M488A SNOMED CT 83561009 = lateral/root-canal spinal stenosis in the cervical region. SNOMED CT
        has no region-specific lateral spinal stenosis concept: the only lateral-stenosis concepts are
        40521992 (316910006) which is a non-region-specific UK-extension concept, and SNOMED CT's maps_to
        for that points to 4116359 (an placeholder, not a clinical standard). The best region-specific
        clinical standard concept is therefore SNOMED CT 436785 (83561009, Spinal stenosis in cervical
        region), which fully subsumes the source as the parent cervical-stenosis concept. Broader map:
        target subsumes the source but loses the lateral-vs-central distinction. Moderate tier: SNOMED CT
        does not distinguish lateral from central stenosis at this regional level; defensible
        best-available target but with real specificity loss.
        """
}
